hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16056","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Aban ibn Salih, from al-Fadl ibn Abd Allah ibn Maqil ibn Sinan, from Abd Allah ibn Niyar al-Aslami, from Amr ibn Shas al-Aslami, he said, and he was of the companions of al-Hudaybiyah, he said, I went out with Ali to Yemen, and he was harsh to me in that journey of mine, until I found it in myself against him, and when I arrived, I showed my complaint of him in the mosque, until that reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I entered the mosque one morning, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among people of his companions, and when he saw me, he fixed me with his eyes, saying, he sharpened the look to me, until when I sat, he said: O Amr, by Allah, you have hurt me. I said, I seek refuge with Allah from hurting you, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Nay, whoever hurts Ali has hurt me."
